      {
        "id": 138017,
        "name": "adamiani",
        "username": "adamiani",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/90db22/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-02T09:05:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"flyingscotsman2011\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/flyingscotsman2011/48/2476_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> flyingscotsman2011:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I would think Expat is in Gryffindor. Yes, she has a sharp mind and enjoys tinkering with her guns which would make her an alright fit in Ravenclaw, but her play style is less that of a tactical thinker and more of a tank. She is a trained fighter, and she hates backing down from a fight, even if (and she almost seems to enjoy it when) she's the underdog in a fight. She shows that same bravery that we see from Harry, Ron, and even Neville Longbottom in the series, and I think that that bravery is what puts her in Gryffindor. Also, she could put a bullet between Voldemort's eyes before you could say \"Gillie Weed.\" And that mental image makes me very happy :)\"Avada Ke-\"BANG!<em>roll credits</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br>Gryffindor?<br><br>Buddy, she's your worst nightmare… a muggle with a gun.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
